  changelog: "2.0 (2026-08-29)\n- Step sequencer: 64 steps, recorded and played from the preset pads, with rests, ties and 303-style slides.\n- External clock divide: with a clock patched in, the arpeggiator rate knob divides it, /1 to /8.\n- Presets and the sequence survive power-off.\n- Reduced clock jitter.\n- Each preset knob can be assigned individually: note orders, swing, a bank of step patterns, the factory octave switch, or left factory.\n- Preset voltages are set by holding a pad and turning the knob above it.\n- Alternate tunings accept Scala keyboard maps, so a scale can have any number of degrees and repeat at something other than the octave. The octave controls step that period.\n- Leaving the arpeggiator\u2019s latch no longer stops notes still held by hand.\n\n1.2 (2026-08-25)\n- Improved pressure-based portamento behavior.\n- Held-key state is cleared on the first boot after flashing, so a stuck gate no longer survives an update.\n\n1.1 (2026-08-21)\n- trn and remote enable stay factory when nothing has taken them.\n- The macOS flasher is a signed, notarised app.\n\n1.0 (2026-08-19)\n- Initial release.\n",
